      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that it's complex, but that's kinda a vague answer for a paper. if you had to look at the data, isn't it pretty much a consensus that these types of big trade deals mostly benefited corporations and high-level execs while leaving actual blue-collar workers behind? like, the job losses in manufacturing aren't really a \"debate,\" they're just a fact.",
